 [rel('gender','Examines how colonial classification produced unequal models of feminine respectability around prostitution.',[sid('levine_article')],'Primary abstract and printed pp. 5–7 read, rather than publisher blurb. Historical official categories remain objects of critique, not labels endorsed by this entry; no full monograph reading.'),rel('racial_formation','Connects colonial sociological measurement and sexual classification to the production of racial hierarchy.',[sid('levine_article')],'The same primary opening develops official counting and differentiated knowledge about colonized populations. The argument concerns British India in the nineteenth and early twentieth centuries, not a uniform claim about every empire.')],
